activation	Print prompt	2026-10-28T05:20:42.4097815Z {"title": "Error message on missing column lacks essential details", "body": "### What happens?\n\nAs indicated in upstream reference: duckdb/duckdb/discussions/22301, when `read_parquet` is used on multiple files it uses the first read files to guess the schema, including which columns are there if `union_by_name=false`.\n\nWhen reading another file the schema is incompatible, the error message is quite concise:\n\n```_duckdb.ConversionException: Conversion Error: Unimplemented type for cast (VARCHAR -> \"NULL\")```\n\nthis message does not report *which* column could not be cast, nor on which file, making it quite hard to troubleshoot. I only know that some column in some file was missing; the same thing happens if the column type is different across different files.\n\n### To Reproduce\n\nExample code (sadly the data on which I found this is private, but I think the issue is quite clear even without reproducing it).\n\n```\nSELECT DISTINCT x\nFROM read_parquet('s3://my-bucket/data/**/*.parquet')\nWHERE y = 123\n```\n\n### OS:\n\nall\n\n### DuckDB Version:\n\n1.5.2\n\n### DuckDB Client:\n\npython\n\n### Hardware:\n\n_No response_\n\n### Full Name:\n\nJacopo Farina\n\n### Affiliation:\n\nFlixbus\n\n### Did you include all relevant configuration (e.g., CPU architecture, Linux distribution) to reproduce the issue?\n\n- [x] Yes, I have\n\n### Did you include all code required to reproduce the issue?\n\n- [x] Yes, I have\n\n### Did you include all relevant data sets for reproducing the issue?\n\nNo - I cannot share the data sets because they are confidential"}
